Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.53,0:00:02.98,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Your... revenge?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.45,0:00:09.74,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,We're going to send every last one of the \Nscoundrels who had me executed to hell.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.74,0:00:10.68,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.68,0:00:14.74,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,W-Well... Who exactly are they?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.74,0:00:16.35,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,I don't know.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.90,0:00:19.69,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,How could I? I was set up.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.69,0:00:22.86,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,I was executed for poisoning Cecilia,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.86,0:00:27.00,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,but I would obviously never \Nresort to anything so pedestrian.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.00,0:00:29.50,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,You mean... you were innocent?!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.50,0:00:31.51,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Which is why, Constance,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.22,0:00:37.54,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,you will become my agent, \Nunmask the true culprit...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.54,0:00:40.01,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,and give them a taste of hell on earth!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.01,0:00:42.83,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I c-couldn't possibly.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.83,0:00:45.09,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,I know your family is in debt.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.09,0:00:48.24,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,What will you do now that \Nyou've broken off your engagement?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.24,0:00:50.39,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,I didn't! That wasn't me!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.39,0:00:52.52,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,{\i0}You're{\i1} the one who did that!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.52,0:00:54.02,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Moreover...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.02,0:00:57.86,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Does refusing to repay me \Nfor assisting you yesterday
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.86,0:01:00.79,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,{\i1}sound{\i0} like "Grail sincerity" to you?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.59,0:01:06.79,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Wh-What would you have me do?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.97,0:02:44.52,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I b-beg your pardon\N for calling so suddenly.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.87,0:02:48.91,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I've come on behalf of the Orlamundes.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.91,0:02:50.71,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Lettie is my name.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.71,0:02:55.76,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,The family wishes to collect letters from\N the Maurice Home for Orphaned Children
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.76,0:02:58.07,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,to commemorate Lady Lily's death this day.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.07,0:03:00.94,Default,Nun,0,0,0,,Why, the children will be delighted.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.94,0:03:02.48,Default,Nun,0,0,0,,Please, come in.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.82,0:03:07.29,Flashback,Scarlett,0,0,0,,First...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.29,0:03:11.35,Flashback,Scarlett,0,0,0,,You may as well begin by questioning \Nthose who might know what happened.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.35,0:03:13.37,Flashback,Connie,0,0,0,,S-Such as?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.37,0:03:14.80,Flashback,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Let me think...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.06,0:03:18.17,Flashback,Scarlett,0,0,0,,I daresay Lily Orlamunde\Nwill prove useful.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.17,0:03:21.93,Flashback,Connie,0,0,0,,What? Lady Lily? But she's...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:23.26,0:03:25.94,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,Lady Lily was Lady Scarlett's friend.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.43,0:03:28.28,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,Following Lady Scarlett's death,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.28,0:03:31.93,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,she devoted herself to good works \Nto atone for her crimes.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.47,0:03:36.69,Main - Top + Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,People called her the White Lily \Nof Charity for her fairness.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.69,0:03:38.77,Main - Top + Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,I admired her.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.49,0:03:46.82,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,But two years ago, she drank poison and\Nended her own life in her family's chapel.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.82,0:03:49.96,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,Her reasons remain unknown to this day.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.76,0:03:52.75,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,I find that hard to believe.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.75,0:03:55.70,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,That ill-natured woman \Nwould never choose suicide.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:55.70,0:03:57.77,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I-Ill-natured?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.77,0:04:00.22,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Weren't the two of you\N friends from childhood?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.22,0:04:02.88,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Don't suggest anything so dreadful!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.88,0:04:07.21,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,I'd sooner do a handstand dance on \Na cliff's edge than keep company with her!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.21,0:04:14.73,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,B-But Lady Lily often visited you \Nin prison when no one else would.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.73,0:04:16.38,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Visited me?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.38,0:04:18.25,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Oh, {\i1}those{\i0} visits.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.03,0:04:22.79,Flashback,Lily,0,0,0,,You got careless, Scarlett.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.36,0:04:27.25,Flashback,Scarlett,0,0,0,,I never tried to poison Cecilia.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.25,0:04:28.86,Flashback,Lily,0,0,0,,I don't doubt that.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.86,0:04:31.40,Flashback,Lily,0,0,0,,But that only makes things worse.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.93,0:04:37.53,Flashback,Lily,0,0,0,,It means someone out there is capable \Nof framing a woman of your caliber.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.95,0:04:41.91,Flashback,Lily,0,0,0,,And we still haven't any idea who.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.24,0:04:45.92,Flashback,Lily,0,0,0,,So I've come today to bid you farewell.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.22,0:04:48.15,Flashback,Lily,0,0,0,,Loath as I am to admit it,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.15,0:04:50.68,Flashback,Lily,0,0,0,,I think this business is beyond me.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.79,0:04:53.50,Flashback,Lily,0,0,0,,Do forgive me.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.50,0:04:56.98,Flashback,Lily,0,0,0,,I would have liked to aid you if possible,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.09,0:05:02.39,Flashback,Lily,0,0,0,,but I value my own neck\N far more than yours.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.45,0:05:06.18,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,If she really did take her own life,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.18,0:05:11.01,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,then events got out \Nof her control in some way.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.41,0:05:16.05,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,This must have some bearing on my revenge.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.05,0:05:17.48,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,My intuition tells me so.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.48,0:05:19.91,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,H-How can you be so confident?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.91,0:05:22.04,Default,Tony,0,0,0,,Wait for me!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.67,0:05:22.04,Main - Top,Girl A,0,0,0,,You're too fast for us!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.45,0:05:26.48,Default,George,0,0,0,,Here.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.22,0:05:29.91,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Thank you all for these letters.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.35,0:05:32.57,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I'll see that they reach Lady Lily.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.57,0:05:33.09,Default,George,0,0,0,,Great.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.09,0:05:33.48,Default,Tony,0,0,0,,Hey.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.85,0:05:35.91,Default,Tony,0,0,0,,We'd better hurry back, George.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.91,0:05:37.97,Default,George,0,0,0,,Yeah. I know, Tony.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.97,0:05:39.83,Default,George,0,0,0,,Bye, miss!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.77,0:05:44.70,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Our next visit will be \Nto the scene of Lily's suicide.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.70,0:05:47.49,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,I trust you remember what to do, girl.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.01,0:06:01.79,Default,Nun,0,0,0,,I'm so sorry. We only have habits.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.02,0:06:04.42,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,No, this will do nicely.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.42,0:06:06.21,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Thank you very much.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.07,0:06:20.57,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Excuse me. I'm from the Maurice \NHome for Orphaned Children.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.57,0:06:22.57,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,In memory of Lady Lily...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.80,0:06:31.49,Default,Butler,0,0,0,,Come in. It's right this way.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.49,0:06:33.03,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Thank you very much.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.07,0:06:37.02,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I th-thought I would die of fright.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.02,0:06:39.11,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Nevertheless, everything went swimmingly.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.75,0:06:53.60,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,This is where Lady Lily met her end.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.95,0:06:56.80,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Over here, I suspect.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.23,0:06:58.27,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Wait...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.60,0:07:01.06,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,What are you doing, girl?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.06,0:07:04.61,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Well, I really ought to pray for her.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.61,0:07:09.32,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Nonsense. Prayers wouldn't please her.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.32,0:07:10.78,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Lily...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.35,0:07:16.61,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,would tell you to hurry up and find out\Nthe truth in that snide way of hers.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.95,0:07:21.12,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,I'm certain she left a clue somewhere,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.60,0:07:25.63,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,and in some infuriating place \Nthat no one would think to check.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.48,0:07:29.64,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Could it be... behind the picture frame?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.97,0:07:31.67,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,That would be just like her.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.13,0:07:34.64,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Wh-What a sacrilegious hiding place.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:35.56,0:07:36.94,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,What's this?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.07,0:07:40.63,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,There's really something here!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.15,0:07:49.51,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Hide it!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.51,0:07:50.65,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,R-Right!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.17,0:08:03.16,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Wha...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.16,0:08:05.66,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,What are {\i1}you{\i0} doing here,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.66,0:08:07.66,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Randolph Ulster?!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.94,0:08:14.29,Flashback,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Lily was married?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.29,0:08:19.09,Flashback,Connie,0,0,0,,Yes. To Earl Randolph Ulster \Nof the House of Richelieu.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.09,0:08:22.63,Flashback,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Randolph? That hidebound stick-in-the-mud?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.63,0:08:24.30,Flashback,Connie,0,0,0,,You know him?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.75,0:08:26.99,Flashback,Scarlett,0,0,0,,He's my nemesis.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.29,0:08:31.82,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,People call him "Lord Death."
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.12,0:08:35.25,Main - Top,Randolph,0,0,0,,I beg your pardon. You're from \Nthe Maurice Home for Orphaned Children?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.82,0:08:39.32,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Y-Yes. M-My name is Lettie.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.32,0:08:42.20,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I've, um, only just started there.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:42.20,0:08:47.09,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,I see. I often played \Nwith a little redheaded boy there.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.09,0:08:49.06,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,George, I think his name was.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.06,0:08:50.21,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Is he well?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:50.55,0:08:52.20,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,O-Of cou—
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.20,0:08:54.71,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Wait. We just visited \Nthe orphanage, remember?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:55.10,0:08:57.56,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,George had chestnut hair.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.56,0:09:00.59,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,The redheaded boy that age \Nwas most certainly Tony.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.15,0:09:05.72,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Um... Could you be thinking \Nof Tony, perhaps?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.96,0:09:11.48,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,There's a younger boy named George, \Nbut he has chestnut hair.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.60,0:09:15.78,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Why, yes. I did mean Tony.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.78,0:09:16.99,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,How rude of me.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.22,0:09:20.11,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,E-Everyone makes mistakes.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.11,0:09:22.26,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Well, if you'll excuse me...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:23.76,0:09:24.99,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Sister.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.75,0:09:28.63,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,The roads are perilous \Nfor a woman walking alone.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.63,0:09:31.14,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,If you permit it, \NI shall see you to the orphanage.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.14,0:09:34.88,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Th-That's all right!\N I, er, have an errand to run.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.88,0:09:36.77,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Although I do appreciate your offer.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.24,0:09:39.26,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,So, good day to you, my lord.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.27,0:09:49.10,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I was scared stiff!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.10,0:09:51.13,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I've never met anyone so intimidating.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.13,0:09:53.67,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,D-Do you think he suspects me?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:53.67,0:09:55.16,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,I wonder.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.04,0:10:01.47,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,That man has always had a keener nose \Nthan was good for him.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.02,0:10:19.54,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,You should have gotten rid of those rags.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:19.87,0:10:22.00,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,When the nuns were nice enough \Nto lend them to me?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.72,0:10:38.51,Default,Tony,0,0,0,,Kiriki kirikuku.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.28,0:10:43.79,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,K-Kirikuki...?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:43.79,0:10:45.54,Default,Boy A,0,0,0,,See? I told you so.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.54,0:10:47.85,Default,George,0,0,0,,You always worry too much, Tony.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:47.85,0:10:50.57,Default,Tony,0,0,0,,Shove it. What do you care?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.57,0:10:52.78,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Tell me, what was that?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.56,0:10:54.68,Default,Tony,0,0,0,,A spell.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.68,0:10:55.79,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,A spell?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:55.79,0:10:59.58,Default,Tony,0,0,0,,Yeah. For spotting bad guys.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.58,0:11:01.79,Default,Tony,0,0,0,,Lady Lily taught it to us.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.79,0:11:04.81,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,She did? When?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:05.54,0:11:07.31,Default,Tony,0,0,0,,Before she died.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:07.80,0:11:09.71,Flashback,Lily,0,0,0,,"Kiriki kirikuku."
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.71,0:11:13.21,Flashback,Lily,0,0,0,,If anything should happen to me
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.21,0:11:17.83,Flashback,Lily,0,0,0,,and people come asking \Nabout me, recite this spell.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:18.29,0:11:22.83,Flashback,Lily,0,0,0,,If they react to it at all, \Nyou'll know they're very bad people.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.50,0:11:28.22,Default,Tony,0,0,0,,If that happens, we're supposed to \Nround up everybody and run for it.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.81,0:11:30.64,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,What does this mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.64,0:11:32.82,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,Could it be...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:33.31,0:11:35.20,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,Lady Lily was murdered?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.91,0:11:43.53,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I'm exhausted.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.14,0:11:48.45,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Shall we open it?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.36,0:11:55.60,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,A key?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.12,0:11:57.47,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,It says...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.23,0:12:03.15,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,"Destroy the Holy Grail of Eris."
Dialogue: 0,0:12:04.61,0:12:06.66,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,The Holy Grail of Eris?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:08.75,0:12:11.50,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,What on earth does that mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.50,0:12:13.49,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Don't ask me.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:13.88,0:12:18.50,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,The paper itself looks like part \Nof a pamphlet for sightseers.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.92,0:12:24.43,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Eris is the goddess of discord \Nand strife in the Myth of Faris.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.43,0:12:27.95,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,She is a wicked deity. \NThey say she drove a nation to ruin.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:28.83,0:12:32.63,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,That's a legend from \NAdelbide's neighboring land.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.10,0:12:37.87,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,"Eris" is also the name I used \Nwhenever I wanted to sample the nightlife.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.87,0:12:39.53,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I-I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.94,0:12:42.60,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Now, what about the key?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.60,0:12:43.67,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Well...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.55,0:12:48.96,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,It has a number on it, but nothing \Nto indicate which workshop it was made in.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.96,0:12:52.59,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I don't think we have enough clues \Nto figure out what it's for.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.03,0:12:54.80,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,True. Still...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.54,0:12:58.20,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,she was no normal woman.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.63,0:13:03.98,Default,Kate,0,0,0,,Should you be out and about so soon?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.16,0:13:07.56,Default,Kate,0,0,0,,After ending your engagement like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.07,0:13:11.80,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,That's right. I did end my engagement.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.80,0:13:14.93,Default,Kate,0,0,0,,The party even made it into the papers.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.93,0:13:16.06,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,The {\i1}papers{\i0}?!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.95,0:13:24.76,Default,Kate,0,0,0,,"Poor Constance Grail proves even a lamb\Nwill charge a hound when provoked."
Dialogue: 0,0:13:24.76,0:13:27.26,Default,Kate,0,0,0,,Or so the {\i1}Mayflower{\i0}'s \Neditorial opined yesterday.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.57,0:13:30.08,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,O-Oh dear.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.39,0:13:34.58,Default,Kate,0,0,0,,And they say Pamela went back\N to her family's domain the next day.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.03,0:13:40.87,Default,Kate,0,0,0,,It's "for her health," but anyone can see \Nshe ran with her tail between her legs.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.87,0:13:42.29,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,You don't say...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:42.89,0:13:44.40,Default,Kate,0,0,0,,As for Neil,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.40,0:13:49.72,Default,Kate,0,0,0,,the Bronson Company's aristocratic\N clients have started a boycott.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.72,0:13:51.60,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Oh, speaking of which,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:52.16,0:13:55.96,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Neil came to apologize \Nand ask my forgiveness this morning.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.96,0:13:59.20,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I told him how to stop \Nthe people coming after them,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.60,0:14:01.57,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,so that should die down soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.57,0:14:04.25,Default,Kate,0,0,0,,I'm sure he was only thinking of himself.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.11,0:14:09.69,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Maybe, but he did apologize, \Neven if he didn't mean it.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.69,0:14:11.86,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Besides, Neil was the one responsible.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:11.86,0:14:15.62,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,The people who work for \Nthe Bronson Company did nothing wrong.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.62,0:14:20.13,Default,Kate,0,0,0,,Connie, you're sincere to a fault.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.41,0:14:23.83,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Listen to her! You should \Nnever have forgiven him.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.31,0:14:25.72,Default,Kate,0,0,0,,Still, Connie...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.38,0:14:30.42,Default,Kate,0,0,0,,You've become an overnight \Ncelebrity, so be careful.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.42,0:14:32.63,Default,Kate,0,0,0,,I mean, where were you yesterday?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.54,0:14:37.39,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Well, um, I wanted to be alone, so...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.93,0:14:43.96,Default,Kate,0,0,0,,It's quite all right.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.96,0:14:46.89,Default,Kate,0,0,0,,I won't pry until\N you feel like telling me.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:46.89,0:14:47.93,Default,Kate,0,0,0,,So...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:48.40,0:14:52.40,Default,Kate,0,0,0,,you'd better come to me\N when you need help.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.73,0:14:54.14,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Kate!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.25,0:14:58.22,Default,Kate,0,0,0,,Anyway, infidelity is just despicable!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.22,0:15:00.78,Default,Kate,0,0,0,,I suppose you'll want nothing \Nto do with men for—
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.78,0:15:04.00,Default,Kate,0,0,0,,My. Isn't this...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.89,0:15:08.17,Default,Kate,0,0,0,,Aha. I see how it is.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.17,0:15:10.93,Default,Kate,0,0,0,,You're already looking to the future!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.91,0:15:13.42,Default,Kate,0,0,0,,This invitation here.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.85,0:15:18.98,Default,Kate,0,0,0,,I hear lots of good-looking folks \Nattend Emilia Godwin's balls.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:18.98,0:15:20.18,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Wait, Kate...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.18,0:15:22.00,Default,Kate,0,0,0,,I don't blame you, Connie!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:22.00,0:15:26.95,Default,Kate,0,0,0,,I read in a novel that only new love \Ncan heal a broken heart!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.95,0:15:28.44,Default,Kate,0,0,0,,I hope you find someone special!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:28.44,0:15:29.43,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,It's not like—
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.67,0:15:31.32,Default,Kate,0,0,0,,Go for it, Connie!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.17,0:15:36.04,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Sh-She's got some strange idea\N in her head.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:38.24,0:15:39.35,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,What is this card?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.80,0:15:44.46,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Her invitations are \Nas tasteless as I remember.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:44.85,0:15:50.18,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,I'm sure she wants you to spark gossip.\N You did cause a scandal.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.18,0:15:53.60,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Are you acquainted with Baroness Godwin?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.60,0:15:56.32,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Yes, I know her well.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.22,0:16:00.73,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,We shall be attending \NEmilia's ball, Constance!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:01.72,0:16:06.29,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,She loves nothing more than talk\Nand the misfortune of others.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.74,0:16:11.04,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,It's been ten years, \Nbut if we play our cards right,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.04,0:16:14.58,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,she'll sing for us like \Na canary in mating season.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.23,0:16:23.25,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Are you ready, Constance?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:25.69,0:16:28.31,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,We have a delightful party ahead of us.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.50,0:16:40.98,Default,Aisha,0,0,0,,Good evening, Emilia.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.63,0:16:43.90,Default,Emilia,0,0,0,,Good evening, Aisha.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:43.90,0:16:45.62,Default,Emilia,0,0,0,,And who might this be?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.76,0:16:48.35,Default,Aisha,0,0,0,,My special someone.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:48.35,0:16:50.71,Default,Emilia,0,0,0,,I-I see...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.74,0:16:58.91,Default,Emilia,0,0,0,,Why, good evening.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:59.53,0:17:02.66,Main - Italics,Emilia,0,0,0,,Gracious. What a disappointment.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.28,0:17:07.84,Main - Italics,Emilia,0,0,0,,She seems more refined than before, \Nbut she's still a far cry from Scarlett.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:08.87,0:17:13.50,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Thank you very much for inviting me \Nthis evening, Lady Godwin.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:14.78,0:17:16.92,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,What a lovely dress you're wearing.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.60,0:17:23.06,Default,Connie; Scarlett,0,0,0,,With your hair like sunflowers, \Nit suits you perfectly.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.49,0:17:29.43,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,H-Huh? Did I say something wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:29.88,0:17:32.38,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,But I did just what you told me to...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:32.38,0:17:33.64,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Dear me.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.64,0:17:36.41,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,She's just as timid as I remember.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.84,0:17:43.72,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,What now? Emilia left.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.72,0:17:44.57,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,My!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:44.57,0:17:46.63,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,There's Aisha Spencer.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.63,0:17:48.78,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,How she's changed.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.03,0:17:50.27,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,What perfect timing.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:50.27,0:17:53.25,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,I have business with her. \NGo see what she has to say.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:54.72,0:17:56.55,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I-It's him!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.80,0:18:03.04,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,L-L-Lady Scarlett, this is your cue!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.04,0:18:06.09,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Uh, I think not! I can't stand that man!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.21,0:18:08.99,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,What?!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.32,0:18:11.76,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,How nice to see you again, sister.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.31,0:18:15.26,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I th-think you have the wrong person.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.26,0:18:16.52,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Do I?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:16.81,0:18:20.33,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Just the other day, I met a nun \Nwho spoke with no accent,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:20.33,0:18:22.24,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,had unblemished hands,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:22.67,0:18:25.40,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,and curtsied like a lady.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:27.17,0:18:28.21,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,In addition...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.21,0:18:34.17,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,she had hazel hair \Nand bright green eyes just like you.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.43,0:18:36.35,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,C-Coincidences do happen.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.35,0:18:39.76,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,In that case, I'll be direct,\N Constance Grail.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.76,0:18:41.72,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,What are you after?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.08,0:18:45.06,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,What did you take from the chapel?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.06,0:18:48.20,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,My late wife's will? Or something else?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.20,0:18:50.56,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Oh, no, you see...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.83,0:18:53.51,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,S-Somebody save me!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.51,0:18:56.44,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Oh, honestly! Must I do everything?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:56.44,0:18:57.49,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Stand aside,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:57.49,0:18:58.75,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Constance!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.07,0:19:04.08,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,What's the matter?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.62,0:19:07.32,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,You sound terribly certain.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:07.64,0:19:10.29,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,I trust you have proof, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:11.29,0:19:13.29,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Lady Scarlett!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:13.65,0:19:18.54,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,Surely you wouldn't treat a delicate girl\N like a thief without good reason.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.15,0:19:21.79,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,I can't think what I've done \Nto deserve such an insult.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:21.79,0:19:25.30,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Then shall we pay the Maurice Home \Nfor Orphaned Children another visit?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.68,0:19:28.43,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,If they can confirm
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.43,0:19:33.15,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,you are not the same Lettie who \Ncame on behalf of the Orlamundes,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:33.15,0:19:35.32,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,I will admit that I was mistaken.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:35.32,0:19:37.72,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,He knows everything!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.72,0:19:39.33,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,I must decline.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.64,0:19:42.38,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,While I'm honored by your interest,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:42.38,0:19:48.82,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,I value myself too highly to arrange\Na date with a gentleman I've just met.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:00.87,0:20:03.85,Default,Margot,0,0,0,,She brought it on herself, the whore!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:03.85,0:20:05.58,Default,Margot,0,0,0,,She took my husband!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:06.41,0:20:08.16,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Wh-Who are they?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.16,0:20:10.70,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,Teresa Jennings and Margot Tudor.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:11.10,0:20:15.76,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,It would seem Teresa was having \Nan affair with Margot's husband.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:15.76,0:20:16.61,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,What?!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:17.60,0:20:19.89,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,The wound doesn't look deep.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.86,0:20:23.43,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,We should still clean it to be safe.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:19.89,0:20:20.86,Default,Servant,0,0,0,,Are you all right?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:29.82,0:20:33.60,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,I won't pursue the matter further today.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:34.94,0:20:36.12,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,That said...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.12,0:20:39.63,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Can you honestly tell me\N you aren't involved?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.56,0:20:46.13,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,So much for that party.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.13,0:20:49.34,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,And here I'd hoped \Nto question Emilia and Aisha.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.60,0:21:00.36,Default,Emilia,0,0,0,,You remind me of someone.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.89,0:21:04.66,Default,Emilia,0,0,0,,Only you look nothing like her.\N Silly, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:05.18,0:21:07.16,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,You mean Scarlett Castiel?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:08.30,0:21:12.15,Default,Emilia,0,0,0,,I suppose saying such things \Nto an ordinary girl like you
Dialogue: 0,0:21:12.56,0:21:15.12,Default,Emilia,0,0,0,,will earn me another tongue-lashing.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:17.56,0:21:21.67,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Ten years ago,\N why was Scarlett put to death?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:21.67,0:21:23.09,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Do you know?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:23.47,0:21:27.08,Default,Emilia,0,0,0,,Because she tried to poison \NCrown Princess Cecilia.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:27.08,0:21:28.42,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Still...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:29.73,0:21:31.92,Default,Emilia,0,0,0,,You really do remind me of her.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:36.01,0:21:40.37,Default,Emilia,0,0,0,,The seventh division of inmest Mars.\NAt the old Montrose residence.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:40.37,0:21:41.94,Default,Emilia,0,0,0,,The invitation...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:41.94,0:21:44.95,Default,Emilia,0,0,0,,is in Earl John Doe's hat.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:49.76,0:21:52.44,Default,Emilia,0,0,0,,The winners in life are those who survive.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:53.96,0:22:00.46,Default,Emilia,0,0,0,,So take care that you aren't forced \Nto make an early exit, Constance Grail.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:17.20,0:22:19.09,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Kiriki kirikuku.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:20.02,0:22:22.11,Signs,Signs; title,0,0,0,,AN EXTRAORDINARY VILLAINESS\NAND AN ORDINARY GIRL
Dialogue: 0,0:22:24.07,0:22:28.12,Default,Credits,0,0,0,,{\fad(523,524)\fs14\c&H351F51&\3c&H9985A7&\blur2\shad0\pos(183,290)}Translation:\h\h\h\h\hWilliam Varteresian
Dialogue: 0,0:22:29.79,0:22:33.83,Default,Credits,0,0,0,,{\fad(517,520)\fs14\c&H351F51&\3c&H9985A7&\blur2\shad0\pos(160,320)}Subtitle Timing:\NEdgar Cruz\N\N\NSubtitle Editing:\NRiley Dalton
